  "variable": "urine culture result",
  "knowledge card": "Type": "laboratory finding",
  "knowledge card": "Description: A urine culture result is the laboratory outcome of testing a urine sample for growth of microorganisms, such as bacteria or yeast. It indicates whether an organism is present, and if positive, may identify the organism and sometimes its antibiotic susceptibility. Urine culture results are commonly used to help diagnose urinary tract infection and guide antimicrobial treatment."
